            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary spasm during exercise test (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2027-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We thought chest pain associated with ST segment elevation during exercise test in patients with not significant coronary lesions could be related to coronary spasm. Three patients with mild coronary obstructive lesions underwent coronary arteriography during exercise test. In two patients this hypotesis was supported by angiographic documentation of the coronary spasm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
